Workflow
========

1. Rebase to newer upstream
---------------------------

$ ubuntu/bin/rebase-upstream [REV]

# Update the package files following the rebase
$ ubuntu/bin/update-package--all

# Run checks which should fail if firmware files were added or deleted by the rebase
# Update the package files (ubuntu/package/*/files) accordingly
$ ubuntu/bin/check-package--all

# Commit the package files changes
$ ubuntu/bin/commit-package--all

# Update and commit the changelogs of all packages
$ ubuntu/bin/update-changelog--all
$ ubuntu/bin/commit-release--all


2. Build new orig tarballs and source packages
----------------------------------------------

$ ubuntu/bin/create-orig-tarball--all
$ ubuntu/bin/build-package--all -- -S -sa


3. Review source packages
-------------------------

$ ubuntu/bin/create-debdiff--all
$ ubuntu/bin/review-debdiff--all [--no-whence]


4. Upload new source packages
-----------------------------

# To a PPA
$ ubuntu/bin/dput-package--all ppa:foo/bar

# To the archive (simulated)
$ ubuntu/bin/dput-package--all -s ubuntu

# To the archive (for real)
$ ubuntu/bin/dput-package--all ubuntu


5. No-change rebuild
--------------------

$ ubuntu/bin/update-changelog--all --rebuild
$ ubuntu/bin/commit-release--all
